  "attribution_note": "Classical rectangular cells and guillotine-layer composition, with no finite published donor packing. PingYou Ltd supplies the explicit finite whole-owner assemblies and certificates.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "complete_mixed_axis_prism_layer_return",
   "proof": "COMPLETE MIXED-AXIS LAYER COMPOSITION\n\nContinue the rectangular-column construction by retaining its complete\nbox, but allow the three cyclic coordinate frames. These are fixed proper\n120-degree rotations about the (1,1,1) axis, not variable prism angles.\n\nFor an owner box with side lengths d0,d1,d2, a layer of type k has complete\nheight dk and contains floor(S/di)*floor(S/dj) whole cells, where i,j are\nthe two other coordinates. An integer word (L0,L1,L2) composes those\nlayers with total height L0*d0+L1*d1+L2*d2. It fits the SAME cube when\nthat sum<=S. The number of owners is the sum of the three layer counts\ntimes their actual in-layer capacities. All layers use common transverse\ncube walls, and adjacent layers share their full horizontal boundary.\nDeleting named whole cells yields any smaller count. This is a complete\nphysical decoder; an independent per-layer enclosing scale is never used.\n\nThe finite probe considers transverse events S=m*di, which determine the\nthree layer capacities, and enumerates integer layer words whose total\nheight is below the current comparison bound. For each word the actual\ncommon side is max(transverse_event,total_height). Thus every tested\nstate is a concrete guillotine composition before any comparison is made.\nThe best among these states is only a result for this compositional family,\nnot a general packing bound. Retain all controls and source words.\n\nNative witnesses use three fixed numeric quaternions. Outward interval\nboxes are recomputed for each quaternion; common rational axis lengths\nare rounded upward enough to contain the corresponding cyclic boxes.\nThe full layer word, grid words, every center and the shared cube are\nretained, so rounding or a changed quaternion cannot silently alter a\nboundary cost. The exact cell proof then applies to all whole owners.\n",
